        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module assesses whether the paper's code could be run on its data, and — because `execute = TRUE` — **actually ran it**. We examined 1 R code file.",
          "#### Run order",
          "The scripts were ordered by their data dependencies (a script writing a file another reads runs first), `source()` calls, and numeric filename prefixes.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Order = 1L, File = \"ok.R\", \"Runs after\" = \"—\", \n    Basis = \"none\"), row.names = c(NA, -1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### File paths",
          "To run against the Psych-DS layout, 1 referenced data path would be rewritten to its new location.",
          "#### Missing inputs",
          "Every data file the code reads is either produced by an earlier script or present in the repository.",
          "#### Execution",
          "**The code was run.** Each script ran in an isolated subprocess against a throwaway copy of the Psych-DS layout, in the run order above, with a 60-second per-script timeout. Of 1 script: 1 ran without error, 0 errored, 0 timed out, 0 were skipped (inputs unavailable), 0 could not run because one of its own dependencies is unavailable, and 0 did not parse. Running against current package versions: a break can reflect version drift, which argues for pinning versions.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"ok.R\", Outcome = \"ran_ok\", Detail = \"\", \n    \"Time (s)\" = 0.3), row.names = c(NA, -1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "*Expand a row below to see the output each script produced.*",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — ok.R (ran_ok)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Output (stdout):**\n````\n> dat <- read.csv(\"data.csv\")\n> t.test(dat$x ~ dat$g)\n\n\tWelch Two Sample t-test\n\ndata:  dat$x by dat$g\nt = -4.0415, df = 4.9592, p-value = 0.01008\nalternative hypothesis: true difference in means between group a and group b is not equal to 0\n95 percent confidence interval:\n -5.731711 -1.268289\nsample estimates:\nmean in group a mean in group b \n            2.0             5.5 \n````\n\n:::\n",
          "#### Reported vs. reproduced",
          "1 statistical test reported in the manuscript text was checked against the extracted analysis output: 1 matched (1 fully, 0 partially) — 100% found.",
          "Some reported values were only found alongside OTHER components after being separated from their own originally-reported neighbours (e.g. a mean split from its own confidence interval). The \"Plausible\" column marks whether that split is well-supported: TRUE when the pieces still trace back to the same underlying variable (via the output's own row labels), FALSE when no such link was found — a FALSE match is not necessarily wrong, but is worth checking against its own Source file/Analysis columns before treating it as confirmed.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Reported = \"t=-4.04 df=4.96 p=0.01\", Found = TRUE, \n    Confidence = \"full\", Plausible = \"yes\", \"Matched values\" = \"t=-4.04, df=4.96, p=0.01\", \n    \"Not matched\" = \"\", \"Source file\" = \"ok.R\", Analysis = \"Welch Two Sample t-test\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n"
        ]
